    {
      "id": "lapo55v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Rise of the Gupta Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Samudragupta was a prominent ruler of the Gupta Empire who reigned from 335 to 375 CE.",
        "Chandragupta II, also known as Vikramaditya, ruled the Gupta Empire from 380 to 415 CE.",
        "The Gupta Period is marked by major advancements in administration, economy, art, architecture, literature, and science.",
        "The study guide covers the complete arc of the empire from its rise to its ultimate decline."
      ],
      "id": "yrjhgkq"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ni63mpe",
      "content": "• The Gupta Empire was founded by Sri Gupta around 240 CE."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ug0c8zd",
      "content": "• The Guptas initially ruled a small kingdom in eastern Uttar Pradesh and Bihar."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3jh8f3f",
      "content": "• The real expansion of the empire started with Chandragupta I."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q0g7xj4",
      "content": "• Chandragupta I assumed the title 'Maharajadhiraja'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wpc3sww",
      "content": "• His marriage with Lichchhavi princess Kumaradevi strengthened the Gupta power."
    },
    {
      "id": "2wezok5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Important Gupta Rulers"
